; A segment's duration. First the speaking rate, in hundredths (front/rate.cards, 100 for Klatt's own durations);
; then for each segment x and base (from base.cq), and two lists of factors in hundredths, each ended by 0 (rules
; 2-7 at INP la, rules 9-10 at INP lb). pr starts at 100 and is multiplied by each factor in turn; then dur = (x pr
; / 100 + base) rate / 100 ms goes out, a pause's as well as a sound's. y f / 100 is Horner over f's three digits
; c, b, a (SFT 33, SFT 23, SFT 02): c y, SFT 01, + b y, SFT 01, + a y. Each d y is a jump into the row of nine ADD
; y (cells 90-98), which runs on into cell 99 and so back.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            start   INP   rate     03-03: the speaking rate, in hundredths
  04            rec     INP   x        04-07: a segment
  05                    INP   base
  06                    CLA   c100
  07                    STO   pr
  08            la      INP   f        08-25: pr times each factor of both lists
  09                    CLA   f
  10                    SUB   00
  11                    TAC   lb
  12                    CLA   pr
  13                    STO   y
  14                    JMP   mulf
  15                    STO   pr
  16                    JMP   la
  17            lb      INP   f
  18                    CLA   f
  19                    SUB   00
  20                    TAC   dur
  21                    CLA   pr
  22                    STO   y
  23                    JMP   mulf
  24                    STO   pr
  25                    JMP   lb
  26            dur     CLA   x        26-38: dur = (x pr / 100 + base) rate / 100
  27                    STO   y
  28                    CLA   pr
  29                    STO   f
  30                    JMP   mulf
  31                    ADD   base
  32                    STO   y
  33                    CLA   rate
  34                    STO   f
  35                    JMP   mulf
  36                    STO   d
  37                    OUT   d
  38                    JMP   rec
  39            mulf    CLA   99       39-69: y f / 100
  40                    STO   ret
  41                    CLA   f
  42                    SFT   33
  43                    STO   d
  44                    CLA   cj
  45                    SUB   d
  46                    STO   j1
  47                    CLA   z
  48            j1      DATA  0        (JMP 99-c)
  49                    SFT   01
  50                    STO   t
  51                    CLA   f
  52                    SFT   23
  53                    STO   d
  54                    CLA   cj
  55                    SUB   d
  56                    STO   j2
  57                    CLA   t
  58            j2      DATA  0        (JMP 99-b)
  59                    SFT   01
  60                    STO   t
  61                    CLA   f
  62                    SFT   02
  63                    STO   d
  64                    CLA   cj
  65                    SUB   d
  66                    STO   j3
  67                    CLA   t
  68            j3      DATA  0        (JMP 99-a)
  69            ret     DATA  0
  70            x       DATA  0
  71            base    DATA  0
  72            pr      DATA  0
  73            f       DATA  0
  74            y       DATA  0
  75            d       DATA  0
  76            t       DATA  0
  77            z       DATA  0
  78            c100    DATA  100
  79            cj      JMP   99
  80            rate    DATA  0
  90            row     ADD   y        90-98: the row of nine ADD y, into 99
  91                    ADD   y
  92                    ADD   y
  93                    ADD   y
  94                    ADD   y
  95                    ADD   y
  96                    ADD   y
  97                    ADD   y
  98                    ADD   y
